From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] replay: consult the replay table when replay starts

Replay is a mode, entered by loading a recording, not a capability. What
it allows is one table (replay-conflicts.c, in the overlay): starting a
recording, guest-visible mutation outside the log and fast restore are
refused; hypercall answers and device input come from the log; taint and
observe-only analysis are allowed. Features consult it when requested.
When replay starts (x-rr-begin-replay, or -icount rr=replay at startup),
replay_start_check() refuses what is already in use and replay would
refuse: today, mutating callbacks and a KVM hypercall consumer, the check
these call sites made themselves.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
Origin: new
---
 replay/replay-begin.c | 2 +-
 replay/replay.c       | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/replay/replay-begin.c b/replay/replay-begin.c
index 4d7f7297acc3d01f6d19c1106c026a3a9f7acdb7..18f7c337f94bfe2fad4712e0a3c8a3052be0b537 100644
--- a/replay/replay-begin.c
+++ b/replay/replay-begin.c
@@ -353,7 +353,7 @@ RrBeginRecordInfo *qmp_x_rr_begin_replay(const char *snapshot,
         error_setg(errp, "start the replaying VM paused (-S)");
         return NULL;
     }
-    if (!panda_callbacks_replay_safe(errp) || !panda_hypercall_replay_safe(errp)) {
+    if (!replay_start_check(errp)) {
         return NULL;
     }
     if (replay_check_blockers(errp)) {
diff --git a/replay/replay.c b/replay/replay.c
index a68c70f5637999cb0f5e7a9ea11ce00567c02880..2ecce01d52e6da1100a0a97c9b1c1749cbd09ab8 100644
--- a/replay/replay.c
+++ b/replay/replay.c
@@ -515,7 +515,7 @@ void replay_start(void)
     }
     if (replay_mode == REPLAY_MODE_PLAY) {
         Error *err = NULL;
-        if (!panda_callbacks_replay_safe(&err) || !panda_hypercall_replay_safe(&err)) {
+        if (!replay_start_check(&err)) {
             error_reportf_err(err, "Replay: ");
             exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
         }
